# Original summaries (Elite Consulting). key -> (summary paragraphs, key ideas)
S={
'THINK GROW RICH':(["Published in 1937, Think and Grow Rich distills Napoleon Hill's two decades of interviews and study of successful Americans into a practical philosophy of achievement. Hill argues that riches, whether money or other forms of fulfilment, begin as a state of mind, and that anyone who learns to direct their thinking can turn a definite purpose into a concrete result.","The book is built around thirteen steps, beginning with a burning desire and continuing through faith, autosuggestion, specialised knowledge, imagination, organised planning, decision, persistence and the Master Mind. Hill illustrates each principle with stories from business and invention, presenting them as a repeatable process rather than a matter of luck.","Its final chapters turn inward, describing the subconscious mind, the brain as a receiver of ideas, the 'sixth sense' of intuition, and the six basic fears (poverty, criticism, ill health, loss of love, old age and death) that keep people from acting. Overcoming those fears is presented as the precondition for applying everything else."],
 ["Every achievement starts with a definite, burning desire","Write down a specific goal, a deadline and a plan, and review it daily","Persistence and quick decisions separate achievers from the rest","A Master Mind group multiplies knowledge and energy","Fear, especially of poverty and criticism, must be mastered first"]),
'LAW OF SUCCESS IN 16 LESSONS':(["The Law of Success (1928) is Napoleon Hill's original, comprehensive course on achievement, written before Think and Grow Rich and far longer. It is organised as sixteen lessons, each devoted to one principle that Hill identified in the careers of leading industrialists, inventors and statesmen.","The early lessons establish the foundation: the Master Mind alliance, a definite chief aim, self-confidence, the habit of saving and initiative with leadership. The middle lessons cover the creative and personal forces of imagination, enthusiasm, self-control, doing more than you are paid for and a pleasing personality.","The closing lessons deal with accurate thinking, concentration, cooperation, the lessons hidden in failure, tolerance and the Golden Rule. Together they form a full curriculum on how character, habits and clear thinking combine to produce lasting success. The podcast presents the course in three parts."],
 ["Success is a learnable system of sixteen principles","A definite chief aim gives every other principle direction","Doing more than you are paid for compounds over time","Failure is often a temporary defeat that carries a lesson","Cooperation and the Master Mind outperform individual effort"]),
'MASTER KEY TO SUCCESS':(["In this later work Napoleon Hill condenses his philosophy into a short, accessible series of principles intended as a 'master key' to personal achievement. It revisits the ideas he refined over a lifetime of teaching and presents them as a compact program for daily practice.","Hill emphasises definiteness of purpose, the Master Mind principle, going the extra mile and applied faith as the core of the system, supported by self-discipline, enthusiasm, accurate thinking and a pleasing personality. Each principle is shown as reinforcing the others.","The result is an overview of Hill's mature thinking: success is less a matter of talent than of consistently applying a small set of habits until they become second nature."],
 ["Definiteness of purpose is the starting point","Going the extra mile builds reputation and opportunity","Applied faith turns belief into action","Self-discipline makes the other principles stick"]),
'SUCCESS HABITS':(["Success Habits collects material from Napoleon Hill's lectures of the early 1950s, in which he explained his philosophy to live audiences in a direct, conversational style. It reads as a practical guide to turning principles into habits.","Hill walks through definiteness of purpose, the Master Mind, applied faith, going the extra mile, a pleasing personality, accurate thinking, self-discipline and the related principles of his system, giving examples of how each one operates in ordinary careers.","The underlying message is that success comes from repeated behaviour. By deliberately practising these principles until they become automatic, a person reshapes both character and circumstances."],
 ["Habits, not occasional effort, create success","Clarify your purpose and master it daily","Accurate thinking separates facts from opinion","Self-discipline governs emotion and action"]),
'OUTWITTING THE DEVIL':(["Written in 1938 but kept unpublished for decades, Outwitting the Devil is Napoleon Hill's most unusual book: an imagined interview in which Hill questions 'the Devil' about how people are kept in fear, doubt and failure.","The interview form is a device for exploring psychological traps: drifting without purpose, letting others think for you, procrastination and the habit of accepting circumstances. Hill contrasts 'drifters' with people who think independently and act on definite goals.","The book argues that the remedy lies within each person: definiteness of purpose, self-mastery, learning from adversity and using time well. It is both a motivational work and a critique of the institutions and habits that discourage independent thought."],
 ["Drifting through life without a definite aim is the main trap","Fear and procrastination are habits that can be broken","Independent thinking protects against manipulation","Every adversity carries the seed of an equivalent benefit"]),
'GOLDEN RULES':(["The Golden Rules gathers lesser-known essays and editorials by Napoleon Hill, many of them from the magazines he published around the time of the First World War. They show his ideas in an early, compact form.","The pieces address themes such as service, cooperation, self-confidence, the value of a definite aim and the ethic of treating others as you wish to be treated. Hill treats the Golden Rule not only as morality but as a practical principle of business and leadership.","Taken together the essays present success as inseparable from character: lasting achievement depends on the goodwill and trust one builds with others."],
 ["Service and fairness are practical business principles","A definite aim focuses energy","Self-confidence can be cultivated","Character underpins lasting success"]),
'SUCCESS THROUGH POSITIVE MENTAL ATTITUDE':(["Co-written by Napoleon Hill and insurance entrepreneur W. Clement Stone in 1960, this book centres on one idea: a positive mental attitude (PMA) is the catalyst that makes every other success principle work.","Through many short case studies the authors show how people turned setbacks into opportunities by changing the way they interpreted events. They introduce practical tools such as self-motivators, definite goals, study and planning time, and the habit of turning a problem into an advantage.","The book also covers money, health, work and relationships, treating attitude as something that can be chosen and trained. Its message is that while circumstances may be outside our control, our response to them is not."],
 ["Attitude is the deciding factor in outcomes","Use self-motivators to act immediately","Every adversity can be turned into an advantage","Set clear goals and review them regularly"]),
'AS A MAN THINKETH':(["James Allen's short essay of 1903 is one of the founding texts of modern self-help. Taking its title from Proverbs, it argues that a person's character and circumstances are the outward product of their habitual thoughts.","Allen explains that circumstances do not make a person but reveal them, that health and body are influenced by the mind, that purpose gives thought strength, and that achievement follows disciplined, focused thinking. He presents this as a law of cause and effect in the inner life.","The book ends with a meditation on serenity: the calm, self-controlled mind is described as the fruit of long self-mastery and the true foundation of influence and peace."],
 ["Thoughts shape character and circumstances","Purpose gives direction and strength to the mind","Self-control and patience lead to achievement","Calmness is a sign of mastery"]),
'MASTERY OF DESTINY':(["In The Mastery of Destiny (1909), James Allen extends the ideas of As a Man Thinketh into a fuller discussion of how deeds, character and destiny are linked. He argues that destiny is not fixed fate but the accumulated result of our own actions.","Allen discusses the training of the will, thoroughness in work, the building of character through repeated acts, the power of concentration and the importance of self-control. Each is presented as a step toward directing one's own life.","The book closes with an emphasis on meditation and inner discipline. The person who governs their mind, Allen writes, gradually becomes the master rather than the servant of circumstance."],
 ["Destiny is the sum of our deeds","Thoroughness in small tasks builds character","Will and concentration can be trained","Self-mastery precedes mastery of circumstances"]),
'SCIENCE OF GETTING RICH':(["Wallace D. Wattles' 1910 classic sets out to describe a 'science' of becoming wealthy, arguing that getting rich results from thinking and acting in a 'certain way' rather than from environment, talent or luck.","Wattles proposes that a formless substance underlies all things and responds to clear, persistent mental images held with faith and gratitude. He insists that this must be paired with efficient action in one's present work, giving more in use value than one takes in money.","A distinctive theme is his rejection of competition: Wattles urges readers to be creative rather than competitive and to leave everyone they deal with feeling better off. The book later influenced the modern 'law of attraction' movement."],
 ["Form a clear mental picture of what you want","Hold it with faith and gratitude","Act efficiently every day in your current position","Create rather than compete; give more value than you take"]),
'SCIENCE OF BEING GREAT':(["A companion to The Science of Getting Rich, Wallace D. Wattles' 1910 book applies the same approach to personal greatness rather than wealth.","Wattles argues that every person has access to a universal intelligence and can develop power by thinking independently, acting with integrity and seeing others as equals. He stresses consistent thought, service and acting on one's best judgement in each moment.","The book outlines practical exercises in thinking and conduct, presenting greatness as the gradual result of aligning daily actions with one's highest understanding."],
 ["Greatness is available to anyone who develops it","Think for yourself and act on your best judgement","See and treat others as equals","Consistent daily action builds personal power"]),
'RICHEST MAN IN BABYLON':(["George S. Clason's The Richest Man in Babylon (1926) teaches personal finance through parables set in ancient Babylon. The stories centre on Arkad, a wealthy man who explains how he built his fortune from modest beginnings.","Its best-known lessons are the 'seven cures for a lean purse': save at least a tenth of what you earn, control expenses, make your savings work, guard against loss, own your home, provide for the future and increase your ability to earn. The 'five laws of gold' summarise how money grows or disappears.","The parables also address debt, luck and the value of seeking advice from experienced people. The book remains popular because its rules are simple, concrete and as applicable today as when they were written."],
 ["Pay yourself first: keep at least 10% of income","Make saved money work for you","Avoid risky schemes and seek expert advice","Increase your skill and earning power"]),
'MASTER KEY SYSTEM':(["Charles F. Haanel's The Master Key System began in 1912 as a 24-week correspondence course and became one of the central texts of the New Thought movement.","Each week presents a lesson and an exercise on the relationship between the conscious mind, the subconscious and what Haanel calls the universal mind. Readers practise stillness, concentration and visualisation, gradually learning to hold a clear mental picture.","Haanel argues that thought is creative and that disciplined thinking, combined with action, shapes health, wealth and circumstances. The course format makes it more of a training programme than a book to be read once."],
 ["Thought is a creative force","Daily concentration exercises train the mind","Visualise clearly and hold the image","Harmony with universal principles brings results"]),
'KYBALION':(["The Kybalion, published in 1908 under the pseudonym 'Three Initiates' (widely attributed to William Walker Atkinson), presents a modern interpretation of Hermetic philosophy.","It is structured around seven principles: Mentalism (the All is mind), Correspondence (as above, so below), Vibration, Polarity, Rhythm, Cause and Effect, and Gender. Each is explained as a universal law operating on physical, mental and spiritual planes.","The book then describes 'mental transmutation', the idea that by understanding these laws a person can change mental states, for example by shifting from one pole of a feeling to its opposite. It has strongly influenced modern esoteric and self-help writing."],
 ["Seven Hermetic principles describe how reality works","Everything vibrates and has its opposite pole","Understanding rhythm helps one stay balanced","Mental states can be deliberately transmuted"]),
'GAME OF LIFE HOW TO PLAY IT':(["Florence Scovel Shinn's 1925 book presents life as a game of giving and receiving governed by spiritual law. Drawing on her work as a metaphysical teacher in New York, she argues that whatever we send out in word or deed returns to us.","Shinn explains the law of prosperity, the power of the spoken word, non-resistance, forgiveness, intuition and the importance of faith. Each chapter is illustrated with short anecdotes from her clients.","Her central tool is the affirmation: short, positive statements used to replace fear with confidence. The book remains a classic of New Thought because of its simple, practical tone."],
 ["What you give out returns to you","Words and affirmations shape experience","Non-resistance and forgiveness free energy","Follow intuition and act with faith"]),
'YOUR WORD IS YOUR WAND':(["A sequel to The Game of Life, Florence Scovel Shinn's Your Word Is Your Wand is mainly a collection of affirmations organised by subject.","Shinn groups her statements under themes such as prosperity, success, happiness, love, health, faith, loss and guidance, building on her view that the spoken word has creative power.","The book is meant to be used, not just read: readers select the affirmations relevant to their situation and repeat them until their thinking changes."],
 ["Spoken words have creative power","Use specific affirmations for specific needs","Repetition replaces fearful thoughts","Faith turns words into results"]),
'POWER OF YOUR SUBCONSCIOUS MIND':(["Dr. Joseph Murphy's 1963 bestseller explains how the subconscious mind accepts and acts on the beliefs given to it by the conscious mind.","Murphy describes techniques such as visualisation, affirmation and suggestion before sleep, and shows how they can be applied to health, prosperity, relationships, career and the removal of fear. He illustrates each method with stories of people who changed their lives.","The core message is that by consciously choosing and repeating constructive ideas, a person can reprogram habitual beliefs and thereby change behaviour and results."],
 ["The subconscious acts on what it is convinced of","Use the time before sleep for suggestion","Visualise the desired result as already real","Replace fear with constructive belief"]),
'MAGIC OF BELIEVING':(["Claude M. Bristol, a journalist and businessman, wrote The Magic of Believing in 1948 to explain the power of belief that he had observed in successful people and in his own life.","Bristol describes how repeated suggestion shapes the subconscious, and offers practical techniques: writing goals on cards, using mirrors to strengthen self-confidence, visualising outcomes and surrounding oneself with supportive influences.","He presents belief as a practical tool rather than a mystical idea: what we deeply believe we tend to act on, and our actions shape the results we see."],
 ["Belief drives action and results","Repetition plants ideas in the subconscious","Use cards and mirror technique to reinforce goals","Choose your influences carefully"]),
'SECRET OF THE AGES':(["Robert Collier's The Secret of the Ages (1926) sets out in seven volumes his view that the mind is the ultimate creative power and that anyone can tap it to achieve their desires.","Collier discusses the subconscious as 'the genie of your mind', the role of desire, visualisation, faith and gratitude, and how these apply to health, money and relationships. He blends New Thought metaphysics with the direct style of the advertising copywriter he was.","The book stresses that clear desire, a definite mental image and confident expectation, followed by action, are the 'secret' behind every achievement."],
 ["Desire is the starting point of creation","The subconscious works on clear mental images","Expect the result with faith and gratitude","Follow inspiration with action"]),
'MEDITATIONS':None,
'MARCUS AURELIUS MEDITATIONS':(["The Meditations are the private notebooks of Marcus Aurelius, Roman emperor from 161 to 180 AD, written in Greek for his own guidance and never intended for publication.","Across twelve books he reminds himself of Stoic principles: to accept what is outside his control, to focus on his own judgements and actions, to act for the common good and to remember the brevity of life. The opening book is a list of gratitude to the people who shaped him.","The notes combine philosophy with practical self-discipline. Their honesty about anger, fatigue and duty has made them one of the most widely read guides to calm, responsible leadership."],
 ["Focus on what is within your control","Our judgements, not events, disturb us","Act for the common good","Remember mortality to keep perspective"]),
'SUN TZU':(["The Art of War, attributed to the Chinese general Sun Tzu and dating to around the 5th century BC, is one of the oldest treatises on strategy. It consists of thirteen short chapters.","The chapters cover planning, waging war, attack by stratagem, tactical dispositions, energy, weak and strong points, manoeuvring, variation, the army on the march, terrain, the nine situations, attack by fire and the use of spies. Sun Tzu emphasises knowledge, deception, timing and the avoidance of costly direct conflict.","Its maxims, such as winning without fighting and knowing both yourself and your opponent, have been widely applied in business, negotiation and leadership."],
 ["The best victory is won without fighting","Know yourself and your opponent","Careful planning precedes action","Exploit weaknesses and avoid strengths"]),
'MACHIAVELLIS PRINCE':(["Niccolò Machiavelli wrote The Prince around 1513; it was published in 1532. It is a short handbook on how rulers acquire and keep power, drawing on examples from ancient history and Renaissance Italy.","Machiavelli classifies types of principalities, discusses armies and the dangers of mercenaries, and analyses the qualities a ruler should display. He famously argues that it is safer to be feared than loved if one cannot be both, and that a prince must sometimes act against conventional morality to preserve the state.","The book is valued for its realistic analysis of power and human behaviour, and remains a key text on leadership, politics and strategy."],
 ["Power must be understood as it is, not as we wish it were","Rely on your own forces, not mercenaries","Reputation and perception matter","Adapt to fortune with boldness"]),
'ART OF MONEY GETTING':(["P. T. Barnum, the showman and entrepreneur, published The Art of Money Getting in 1880 as a set of practical rules for earning and keeping money.","His advice includes choosing the right vocation, avoiding debt, persevering, doing work thoroughly, using the best tools, advertising, being polite and honest, and not scattering one's efforts. He warns repeatedly against extravagance and living beyond one's means.","The tone is humorous and anecdotal, but the rules are sound and timeless: earn honestly, spend less than you earn and build a reputation for reliability."],
 ["Choose work that suits you","Avoid debt and live below your means","Advertise and be reliable","Persevere and finish what you start"]),
'MY LIFE WORK':(["My Life and Work (1922), written with Samuel Crowther, is Henry Ford's account of how he built the Ford Motor Company and his philosophy of business.","Ford describes his early experiments, the development of the Model T, the moving assembly line and the five-dollar day. He argues that business should be organised around service and efficiency rather than short-term profit, and that lower prices and higher wages can reinforce each other.","The book also contains his views on finance, labour and management. It is both an industrial history and a statement of principles that shaped twentieth-century mass production."],
 ["Service before profit","Efficiency and simplification lower costs","Higher wages can create customers","Constant improvement of product and process"]),
'AUTOBIOGRAPHY':(["The Autobiography of Andrew Carnegie, published in 1920 after his death, tells the story of a Scottish immigrant boy who became one of the richest men in the world.","Carnegie recounts his childhood in Dunfermline, his family's emigration to Pittsburgh, his rise from bobbin boy to telegraph operator and railway manager, and his move into iron and steel. He describes the people who helped him and the business principles he followed.","The later chapters cover his philanthropy, including libraries, education and peace initiatives, reflecting his belief that wealth should be used for the public good."],
 ["Work hard and seize every chance to learn","Choose good partners and trust capable people","Concentrate your efforts","Wealth carries a duty to give back"]),
'EMPIRE OF BUSINESS':(["The Empire of Business (1902) collects Andrew Carnegie's essays and addresses on business, money and economics.","Carnegie advises young men on the road to success, explains money and currency, discusses the relationship between labour and capital, and comments on railways, steel and trade. His tone is practical and confident.","The essays show how Carnegie connected individual effort with national prosperity, and they contain his recurring advice: concentrate, save, aim high and be thorough."],
 ["Concentrate your energy on one field","Aim high and take responsibility","Understand money and economics","Labour and capital share common interests"]),
'CRYSTALLIZING PUBLIC OPINION':(["Edward L. Bernays, often called the father of public relations, published Crystallizing Public Opinion in 1923. It was one of the first books to define the profession of the public relations counsel.","Bernays explains how public opinion is formed through groups, habits, leaders and media, and how an adviser can help organisations understand and influence it. He draws on psychology and sociology to explain why people accept or reject ideas.","The book is an early study of persuasion and communication, important for understanding modern marketing, politics and media."],
 ["Public opinion is shaped by groups and leaders","Understanding psychology is key to persuasion","Communication must be two-way","PR shapes how organisations are perceived"]),
'SELF MASTERY THROUGH CONSCIOUS AUTOSUGGESTION':(["Émile Coué, a French pharmacist and psychologist, published this short book in 1920, describing the method of conscious autosuggestion he used with thousands of patients.","Coué argues that imagination is stronger than will: when the two conflict, imagination wins. He recommends repeating a general formula, famously 'Every day, in every respect, I am getting better and better', morning and evening, without effort.","The book includes accounts of patients and practical instructions. It remains an important early text on the power of suggestion and positive self-talk."],
 ["Imagination is stronger than willpower","Repeat simple positive formulas daily","Avoid forcing; let suggestion work gently","Self-talk influences health and mood"]),
'EDINBURGH LECTURES ON MENTAL SCIENCE':(["Thomas Troward, a retired judge in British India, delivered these lectures in Edinburgh in 1904. They became a cornerstone of New Thought philosophy.","Troward distinguishes between objective and subjective mind, explains the creative role of thought and discusses the relationship between the individual mind and the universal mind. He uses a logical, almost legal style of argument.","His conclusion is that the individual can consciously cooperate with universal creative law through focused thought and expectation, an idea that influenced many later writers."],
 ["Distinguish objective and subjective mind","Thought is the creative starting point","The individual mind links to universal mind","Expectation shapes outcomes"]),
'FEELING IS THE SECRET':(["Neville Goddard's short 1944 book explains his central teaching: the feeling attached to an idea is what impresses it on the subconscious and brings it into experience.","Goddard discusses the law and its operation, the importance of the state before sleep, prayer as the feeling of the wish fulfilled, and the role of the spirit. He urges readers to assume the feeling of already having what they desire.","The book is concise and practical, and it is often recommended as the best introduction to Neville's work."],
 ["Feeling impresses ideas on the subconscious","Assume the feeling of the wish fulfilled","Use the drowsy state before sleep","Control your feelings to control your experience"]),
'POWER OF AWARENESS':(["In The Power of Awareness (1952) Neville Goddard explains how consciousness and assumption create one's experience. He describes 'I AM' as the awareness of being, the source of all creation.","The book covers assumption, desire, imagination, attention, the role of the will, and the importance of revision, which means reimagining past events the way one wishes they had happened. Short case histories illustrate the method.","Its message is that a person changes their world by changing their concept of themselves and persisting in that new assumption until it becomes fact."],
 ["Your assumptions shape your reality","Attention must be held on the desired state","Revise the past in imagination","Persist until the assumption hardens into fact"]),
'MEDITATIONS ON FIRST PHILOSOPHY':None,
'NEW PSYCHOLOGY HAANEL':(["Charles F. Haanel's The New Psychology (1924) continues the ideas of his Master Key System in a set of essays on the creative power of thought.","Haanel explains the psychology of success, the law of abundance, the Master Mind, the law of attraction and the relationship between the conscious, subconscious and universal mind. He links these ideas to health and business.","The book argues that understanding mental laws allows a person to direct thought deliberately and thereby shape circumstances."],
 ["Thought creates conditions","Abundance follows from right thinking","The Master Mind connects individuals to greater power","Understanding mental law enables control"]),
'CLAUSEWITZS ON WAR':(["Carl von Clausewitz's On War, published in 1832 after his death, is one of the most influential works on military theory. The podcast covers its opening books.","Clausewitz defines war as a continuation of politics by other means, describes the 'friction' and uncertainty of real conflict, and introduces the trinity of passion, chance and reason. He also discusses the theory of war and the elements of strategy.","His focus on uncertainty, purpose and the link between ends and means has made the book relevant to business strategy and leadership as well as military thinking."],
 ["War serves political purposes","Friction and uncertainty shape every plan","Strategy links means to ends","Moral forces matter as much as material ones"]),
'MORALS AND DOGMA':(["Albert Pike's Morals and Dogma of the Ancient and Accepted Scottish Rite of Freemasonry (1871) is a long series of lectures on the symbolism and philosophy behind the degrees of the Scottish Rite.","Pike moves degree by degree, from Apprentice to Sublime Prince of the Royal Secret, drawing on religion, philosophy, Kabbalah, Hermeticism and history. The lectures address duty, justice, truth, toleration, self-discipline and the pursuit of knowledge.","The podcast presents the work degree by degree, so each episode can be heard on its own. Pike's text is dense and erudite, and it is best approached as a survey of the moral and mystical ideas that Freemasonry inherited."],
 ["Each degree teaches a moral and symbolic lesson","Duty, justice and truth form the core","Ancient religions and philosophies are interconnected","Self-improvement is the purpose of initiation"]),
'WISDOM OF LIFE':(["The Wisdom of Life is part of Arthur Schopenhauer's Parerga and Paralipomena (1851) and offers practical advice on how to live as happily as possible.","Schopenhauer divides the sources of happiness into what a person is (personality), what a person has (property) and how a person is regarded (reputation). He argues that personality matters most, because health, intelligence and a calm temperament determine how we experience everything else.","He warns against overvaluing wealth and other people's opinions, and praises independence, leisure and intellectual life as the surest foundations of contentment."],
 ["What you are matters more than what you have","Health and temperament shape happiness","Don't overvalue others' opinions","Inner resources give independence"]),
}
